---
import StandaloneGuide from '../../components/StandaloneGuide.astro';
const sections = [
  { heading:'Plan around four repeatable content jobs', body:'A newsletter calendar gets easier when every send does not need a brand-new concept. Give your emails a small set of repeatable jobs, then rotate them based on what your audience needs.', bullets:['Teach: answer one useful question','Curate: share a short set of links, tools or ideas','Promote: make one clear offer or announcement','Connect: share a story, behind-the-scenes note or point of view'] },
  { heading:'Choose cadence before choosing topics', body:'A realistic cadence is more valuable than an ambitious calendar you abandon. Weekly can work when you have a steady stream of ideas. Twice monthly is often easier for small teams or creators. Monthly works when each send is more substantial. Pick the frequency you can sustain for at least three months.' },
  { heading:'Build the month from business dates backward', body:'Put launches, promotions, events, seasonal deadlines and planned announcements on the calendar first. Then use the remaining sends for education, curation or relationship-building so every email is not asking the reader to buy something.', bullets:['Send date','Primary goal','Audience or segment','Main topic','Primary CTA','Links or assets needed','Subject line ideas','Post-send note'] },
  { heading:'Keep an idea bank separate from the calendar', body:'The calendar should contain committed sends. Your idea bank should contain possibilities. Mixing the two makes a long list feel like an obligation. Capture reader questions, customer conversations and recurring problems in the idea bank, then pull the strongest ideas into actual send dates.' }
];
const checklist=['Choose a sustainable cadence','Mark launches and deadline-driven sends first','Give every send one primary goal','Write one clear CTA','Keep an idea bank outside the calendar','Note required links and assets','Draft subject lines before send day','Add one post-send learning note'];
const mistakes=['Planning a different format for every email','Making every send promotional','Choosing weekly because it sounds better even when capacity is monthly','Putting vague ideas on dates with no clear purpose','Using multiple competing CTAs','Ignoring what readers actually click, reply to or ask about'];
const faqs=[{q:'How do I make a newsletter content calendar?',a:'Choose a realistic cadence, add fixed business dates first, assign one goal and topic to each send, and keep a separate idea bank for future possibilities.'},{q:'How often should a small business send a newsletter?',a:'There is no single best cadence. Weekly, twice monthly or monthly can all work if the schedule is consistent and the emails are useful. Choose the frequency you can sustain.'},{q:'What should I track for each newsletter?',a:'Track the send date, goal, audience, topic, CTA, required links or assets, subject line ideas and a short note on what happened after the send.'}];
---
<StandaloneGuide slug="newsletter-content-calendar" category="newsletter planning" title="Newsletter Content Calendar | Simple Monthly Email Planning System" description="Build a newsletter content calendar with a practical monthly system for send dates, topics, CTAs, launches, idea banks and a sustainable email cadence." h1="How to build a newsletter content calendar that does not start from a blank page every week." intro="A useful newsletter calendar is less about filling boxes and more about reducing repeated decisions. When your cadence, content jobs and business dates are clear, each send has a reason to exist before you start writing." quickAnswer="Pick a sustainable cadence, add launches and deadline-driven emails first, rotate a few repeatable content types, give each send one primary goal, and keep uncommitted ideas in a separate idea bank." relatedDownload="newsletter-planner-template" relatedLabel="Newsletter Planner Template" {sections} {checklist} {mistakes} {faqs} relatedGuides={[{href:'/digital-downloads/creator-media-kit-template/',label:'Creator Media Kit guide'},{href:'/guides/creator-media-kit-sections/',label:'What to include in a creator media kit'}]} />
